{"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Shape2D"],"kind":"relationships"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SQ","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SH","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s12IdentifiableP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VariantConvertible"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A 2D polyline shape used for physics collision."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Class","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot21ConcavePolygonShape2DC","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ConcavePolygonShape2D","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ConcavePolygonShape2D","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConcavePolygonShape2D"}],"modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"symbolKind":"class","role":"symbol"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D\/segments"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D\/godotClassName"],"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ConcavePolygonShape2D","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A 2D polyline shape, intended for use in physics. Used internally in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" when it’s in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D\/BuildMode-swift.enum\/segments"},{"type":"text","text":" mode."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Being just a collection of interconnected line segments, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D"},{"text":" is the most freely configurable single 2D shape. It can be used to form polygons of any nature, or even shapes that don’t enclose an area. However, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hollow"}]},{"text":" even if the interconnected line segments do enclose an area, which often makes it unsuitable for physics or detection.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When used for collision, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is intended to work with static "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionShape2D"},{"type":"text","text":" nodes like "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/StaticBody2D"},{"type":"text","text":" and will likely not behave well for "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CharacterBody2D","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"s or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RigidBody2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"s in a mode other than Static."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Physics bodies that are small have a chance to clip through this shape when moving fast. This happens because on one frame, the physics body may be on the “outside” of the shape, and on the next frame it may be “inside” it. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is hollow, so it won’t detect a collision.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Warning","style":"warning"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Performance:","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Due to its complexity, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is the slowest 2D collision shape to check collisions against. Its use should generally be limited to level geometry. If the polyline is closed, "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D\/BuildMode-swift.enum\/solids","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" mode can be used, which decomposes the polygon into convex ones; see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D","isActive":true},{"text":"’s documentation for instructions.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/concavepolygonshape2d"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/CollisionPolygon2D":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/collisionpolygon2d","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"CollisionPolygon2D","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"CollisionPolygon2D","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A node that provides a polygon shape to a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionObject2D"},{"text":" parent.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CollisionPolygon2D","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/CollisionPolygon2D/BuildMode-swift.enum/segments":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collisions will only include the polygon edges. In this mode the node has the same effect as a single "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D"},{"type":"text","text":" made of segments, with the restriction that each segment (after the first one) starts where the previous one ends, and the last one ends where the first one starts (forming a closed but hollow polygon)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/collisionpolygon2d\/buildmode-swift.enum\/segments","title":"CollisionPolygon2D.BuildMode.segments","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D\/BuildMode-swift.enum\/segments","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"segments","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/CollisionObject2D":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionObject2D","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/collisionobject2d","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Abstract base class for 2D physics objects."}],"title":"CollisionObject2D","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CollisionObject2D","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"CollisionObject2D","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/s12IdentifiableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s12IdentifiableP","title":"Swift.Identifiable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://SwiftGodot/SQ":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SQ","title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/StaticBody2D":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StaticBody2D","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"StaticBody2D","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/staticbody2d","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StaticBody2D"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/StaticBody2D","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A 2D physics body that can’t be moved by external forces. When moved manually, it doesn’t affect other bodies in its path."}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Shape2D":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Shape2D","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Abstract base class for 2D shapes used for physics collision.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Shape2D","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/shape2d","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Shape2D","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Shape2D"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ConcavePolygonShape2D":{"title":"ConcavePolygonShape2D","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/concavepolygonshape2d","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConcavePolygonShape2D","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConcavePolygonShape2D"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A 2D polyline shape used for physics collision.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/RigidBody2D":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A 2D physics body that is moved by a physics simulation."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RigidBody2D","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/rigidbody2d","title":"RigidBody2D","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RigidBody2D","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RigidBody2D"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/CharacterBody2D":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CharacterBody2D"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/characterbody2d","role":"symbol","title":"CharacterBody2D","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A 2D physics body specialized for characters moved by script."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CharacterBody2D","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CharacterBody2D","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ConcavePolygonShape2D/godotClassName":{"kind":"symbol","title":"godotClassName","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"godotClassName"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"StringName","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot10StringNameC"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D\/godotClassName","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/concavepolygonshape2d\/godotclassname"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ConvexPolygonShape2D":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/convexpolygonshape2d","title":"ConvexPolygonShape2D","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ConvexPolygonShape2D","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConvexPolygonShape2D"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A 2D convex polygon shape used for physics collision.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/CollisionPolygon2D/BuildMode-swift.enum/solids":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D\/BuildMode-swift.enum\/solids","type":"topic","title":"CollisionPolygon2D.BuildMode.solids","abstract":[{"text":"Collisions will include the polygon and its contained area. In this mode the node has the same effect as several ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" nodes, one for each convex shape in the convex decomposition of the polygon (but without the overhead of multiple nodes)."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/collisionpolygon2d\/buildmode-swift.enum\/solids","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"solids"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/SH":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SH","title":"Swift.Hashable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/CollisionShape2D":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A node that provides a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Shape2D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" to a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionObject2D"},{"text":" parent.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionShape2D","title":"CollisionShape2D","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CollisionShape2D"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CollisionShape2D"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/collisionshape2d"},"doc://SwiftGodot/s23CustomStringConvertibleP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","title":"Swift.CustomStringConvertible","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/VariantConvertible":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VariantConvertible"}],"role":"symbol","title":"VariantConvertible","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/variantconvertible","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VariantConvertible","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"VariantConvertible"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Protocol for types that can be converted to and from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Variant?"},{"text":" aka ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Godot Variant"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Default implementations are provided for most of the functions.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Example of implementation:"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ConcavePolygonShape2D/segments":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"segments"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot18PackedVector2ArrayC","text":"PackedVector2Array"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The array of points that make up the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D"},{"text":"’s line segments. The array (of length divisible by two) is naturally divided into pairs (one pair for each segment); each pair consists of the starting point of a segment and the endpoint of a segment.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/concavepolygonshape2d\/segments","title":"segments","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D\/segments"}}}